(rs274ngc-arcs.ngc)
(Arc dialect: centre format and radius format, composed to NIST RS274/NGC rules.)
(NOT captured from any application. See the README.)
G17 G21 G90 G94 F1000 (XY plane, millimetres, absolute distance, feed per minute)

(centre format, clockwise: start 0,0 centre 10,0 end 10,10)
G0 X0 Y0
G2 X10 Y10 I10 J0

(centre format, counter-clockwise, back to the origin: start 10,10 centre 10,0)
G3 X0 Y0 I0 J-10

(full circle: end point identical to the start point, so no axis words, only offsets)
G2 I10 J0

(radius format, positive R: the arc turns through less than 180 degrees)
G2 X10 Y10 R10

(radius format, negative R: the arc turns through more than 180 degrees)
G3 X0 Y0 R-10

(I and J are offsets from the ARC START, not from the origin. The arc distance mode is a)
(separate modal group from the distance mode, so G91 below makes the axis words relative)
(but leaves I and J relative to the arc start.)
G0 X10 Y10
G91
G2 X5 Y5 I5 J0
G90

G0 X0 Y0
M2
